\b Guia Step-by-Step: Overseer em Produ\u231?\u227?o\b0\par
\par
\b 1) Arquitetura (desenho)\b0\par
\f1
+-----------------------+        +-------------------------------+\par
| Browser               | ---->  | frontend/pm_payload.json      |\par
| /apps/overseer/PM.html     |        | frontend/pm_details.json      |\par
+-----------+-----------+        +---------------+---------------+\par
            |                                     ^\par
            v                                     | export (15 min)\par
+----------------------+                  +-------+----------------+\par
| Nginx                |                  | scripts/export_payload |\par
+----------------------+                  +-------+----------------+\par
                                                   |\par
                                                   v\par
                                            +------+------+\par
                                            | MySQL/Maria |\par
                                            | logs + ...  |\par
                                            +------+------+\par
                                                   ^\par
                                 +-----------------+-----------------+\par
                                 |                                   |\par
                         +-------+--------+                   +------+--------+\par
                         | Runner A       |                   | Runner B      |\par
                         | orchestrator   |                   | orchestrator  |\par
                         +----------------+                   +---------------+\par
\f0
\par
\b 2) Estrutura obrigat\u243?ria\b0\par
\f1
pipelines/<pipeline_id>/\par
  pipeline.yaml\par
  src/main.py\par
  config/\par
  secrets/\par
\f0
\par
\b 3) runner_host\b0\par
- auto ou vazio = hostname local\par
- any = qualquer runner\par
- host-a = runner fixo\par
\par
\b 4) Comandos essenciais\b0\par
\f1
python orchestrator.py list\par
python orchestrator.py run <pipeline_id>\par
python scripts/export_payload_from_db.py\par
python orchestrator.py trigger enqueue <pipeline_id> --by <user>\par
python orchestrator.py trigger consume --runner $(hostname -s) --max 20\par
\f0
\par
\b 5) Cron de produ\u231?\u227?o\b0\par
\f1
*/15 * * * * cd /opt/overseer && .venv/bin/python scripts/export_payload_from_db.py >> runtime/logs/export.log 2>&1\par
10 2 * * * cd /opt/overseer && .venv/bin/python scripts/archive_logs.py --days 30 >> runtime/logs/archive.log 2>&1\par
* * * * * cd /opt/overseer && .venv/bin/python orchestrator.py trigger consume --runner $(hostname -s) --max 20 >> runtime/logs/trigger_consume.log 2>&1\par
\f0
\par
\b 6) Nginx (URL final)\b0\par
Servir o path: \f1/apps/overseer/PM.html\f0\par
Root recomendado: \f1/opt/overseer\f0\par
\par
\b 7) Checklist final\b0\par
1. logs recebe runs novas\par
2. frontend/pm_payload.json atualiza\par
3. frontend/PM.html mostra dados\par
4. lineage e run_id_pipeline vis\u237?veis\par
\par
\b 8) Docs para enviar a outra IA\b0\par
- docs/PRD_PM_Universal_DropIn_AI_Ready.md\par
- docs/AI_HANDOFF_CHECKLIST.md\par
- AGENTS.md\par
- README.md\par
- pipelines/_template/\par
}


